# 18. Common `umask` Values

## `umask 022`

Very common default.

New regular files:

```text
644
```

New directories:

```text
755
```

Useful when files should generally be readable by others.

---

## `umask 027`

Typical result:

Files:

```text
640
```

Directories:

```text
750
```

This means:

```text
Owner  → full appropriate access
Group  → read/execute
Others → no access
```

Useful in environments where group members need access but other users should not.

---

## `umask 077`

New files:

```text
600
```

New directories:

```text
700
```

This is useful for private or sensitive data.

